[{:db/id "de54362b-6031-500a-b509-e99fd59af211" :answer/id #uuid "de54362b-6031-500a-b509-e99fd59af211" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{2} u^{4} v^{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "99db7d55-0ba4-574a-abd0-fad22dde97d8" :answer/id #uuid "99db7d55-0ba4-574a-abd0-fad22dde97d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4 u^{4} v^{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "86ac4b28-467b-52f4-b7a3-2b20dd726a36" :answer/id #uuid "86ac4b28-467b-52f4-b7a3-2b20dd726a36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{2} u^{5} v^{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8459c7ad-2f1c-54bb-b579-d98e4986a65b" :answer/id #uuid "8459c7ad-2f1c-54bb-b579-d98e4986a65b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{2} u^{5} v^{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "81a4a4d4-c10a-55dc-b43b-8853d6f328f1" :answer/id #uuid "81a4a4d4-c10a-55dc-b43b-8853d6f328f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "128 u^{6} v^{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "24f470c7-3e68-5664-8116-49ea2082cafa" :answer-field/id #uuid "24f470c7-3e68-5664-8116-49ea2082cafa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["de54362b-6031-500a-b509-e99fd59af211" "99db7d55-0ba4-574a-abd0-fad22dde97d8" "86ac4b28-467b-52f4-b7a3-2b20dd726a36" "8459c7ad-2f1c-54bb-b579-d98e4986a65b" "81a4a4d4-c10a-55dc-b43b-8853d6f328f1"] :answer-field/correct "86ac4b28-467b-52f4-b7a3-2b20dd726a36" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "1d9ba2e0-102f-5ae7-abb7-4c8e12292bfc" :question/id #uuid "1d9ba2e0-102f-5ae7-abb7-4c8e12292bfc" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x^{2} y^{2} z^{2}$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u^{2},\\,v,\\,v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ Assume $u\\geq0.$ What is the missing expression? Choose an integrand equal to the required expression as a function on $D$.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=4 \\sqrt{2} u.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=4 \\sqrt{2} u.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x^{2} y^{2} z^{2})\\,{|}_{x=2 u^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =(2 u^{2}\\cdot 2 u^{2})\\cdot v^{2}\\cdot v^{2} \\\\  & =4 u^{4} v^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4 \\sqrt{2} u 4 u^{4} v^{4}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["24f470c7-3e68-5664-8116-49ea2082cafa"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "33bb8fed-592d-5e3a-8930-5d28957eefc1" :answer/id #uuid "33bb8fed-592d-5e3a-8930-5d28957eefc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1} \\left(- 4 u^{2} - v^{3} + v^{2} \\left(u + v\\right)\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "da65ba3f-7987-5418-bed4-7007a24d71df" :answer/id #uuid "da65ba3f-7987-5418-bed4-7007a24d71df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} + 1 \\left(u + v\\right) v^{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "34bd55fd-9014-5837-a3ed-30210221cafa" :answer/id #uuid "34bd55fd-9014-5837-a3ed-30210221cafa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1} \\left(- 4 u^{2} - 2 v^{3} + v^{2} \\left(u + v\\right)\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "030d3593-551c-5780-836c-e6aa7edd6559" :answer/id #uuid "030d3593-551c-5780-836c-e6aa7edd6559" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(- 4 u^{2} + 1 \\left(u + v\\right) v^{2}\\right) \\left(8 v^{2} + 1\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1c567497-6459-5620-830a-356a99490e90" :answer/id #uuid "1c567497-6459-5620-830a-356a99490e90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(- 4 u^{2} + 1 \\left(u + v\\right) v^{2}\\right) \\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "11fa6424-029e-5a79-821e-cb2a038e5fda" :answer-field/id #uuid "11fa6424-029e-5a79-821e-cb2a038e5fda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["33bb8fed-592d-5e3a-8930-5d28957eefc1" "da65ba3f-7987-5418-bed4-7007a24d71df" "34bd55fd-9014-5837-a3ed-30210221cafa" "030d3593-551c-5780-836c-e6aa7edd6559" "1c567497-6459-5620-830a-356a99490e90"] :answer-field/correct "1c567497-6459-5620-830a-356a99490e90" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "2c8c277a-d40b-52fe-8295-ceb48a2d895c" :question/id #uuid "2c8c277a-d40b-52fe-8295-ceb48a2d895c" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=- 4 x^{2} + y z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,u + v,\\,v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression? Choose an integrand equal to the required expression as a function on $D$.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(- 4 x^{2} + y z)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=u + v\\,z=v^{2}} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (u\\cdot u)+(u+v)\\cdot v^{2} \\\\  & =- 4 u^{2} + 1 \\left(u + v\\right) v^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\left(- 4 u^{2} + 1 \\left(u + v\\right) v^{2}\\right) \\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["11fa6424-029e-5a79-821e-cb2a038e5fda"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "bf0da7f6-74c9-595e-935f-fa2d5e17164f" :answer/id #uuid "bf0da7f6-74c9-595e-935f-fa2d5e17164f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(- 3 u^{3} + u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v\\right) \\sqrt{40 u^{2} + 48 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 4 v^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9c93004a-cd83-5a5e-91b3-6afd517b9553" :answer/id #uuid "9c93004a-cd83-5a5e-91b3-6afd517b9553" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(- 3 u^{3} + u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v\\right) \\left(40 u^{2} + 48 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 4 v^{2}\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fdb763ec-517c-56ab-a78d-f970a030bcd1" :answer/id #uuid "fdb763ec-517c-56ab-a78d-f970a030bcd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 3 u^{3} + u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d3279af3-c719-5f48-8397-3cee94b39b27" :answer/id #uuid "d3279af3-c719-5f48-8397-3cee94b39b27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v\\right) \\sqrt{40 u^{2} + 48 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 4 v^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "13b418aa-8f50-529b-a254-a52c443915a0" :answer/id #uuid "13b418aa-8f50-529b-a254-a52c443915a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(3 u^{3} + u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v\\right) \\sqrt{40 u^{2} + 48 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 4 v^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "27483cd1-fc63-57b7-82c5-fd8540038450" :answer-field/id #uuid "27483cd1-fc63-57b7-82c5-fd8540038450" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["bf0da7f6-74c9-595e-935f-fa2d5e17164f" "9c93004a-cd83-5a5e-91b3-6afd517b9553" "fdb763ec-517c-56ab-a78d-f970a030bcd1" "d3279af3-c719-5f48-8397-3cee94b39b27" "13b418aa-8f50-529b-a254-a52c443915a0"] :answer-field/correct "bf0da7f6-74c9-595e-935f-fa2d5e17164f" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "7d206b38-df94-5588-845c-04813c06e146" :question/id #uuid "7d206b38-df94-5588-845c-04813c06e146" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x - y^{2} z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u v,\\,- u,\\,3 u - v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression? Choose an integrand equal to the required expression as a function on $D$." :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3 u - v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 v,\\,-1,\\,3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3 u - v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 u,\\,0,\\,- 2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 v & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 u & 0 & - 2 v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & - 2 v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 v & 3 \\\\ 2 u & - 2 v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 v & -1 \\\\ 2 u & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 v,\\,6 u + 4 v^{2},\\,2 u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨2 v,\\,6 u + 4 v^{2},\\,2 u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2 v)^{2}+(6 u + 4 v^{2})^{2}+(2 u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40 u^{2} + 48 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 4 v^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x - y^{2} z)\\,{|}_{x=2 u v\\,y=- u\\,z=3 u - v^{2}} \\\\  & =2 u v-1\\cdot (- u)^{2}\\cdot (3 u - v^{2}) \\\\  & =- 3 u^{3} + u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\left(- 3 u^{3} + u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v\\right) \\sqrt{40 u^{2} + 48 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 4 v^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["27483cd1-fc63-57b7-82c5-fd8540038450"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "6f08a77f-a760-599a-8653-c3042e189d26" :answer/id #uuid "6f08a77f-a760-599a-8653-c3042e189d26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 81 u^{3} + 54 u^{2} v^{2} + u v" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "473df280-9c01-54be-9ab5-5f9b35d7d479" :answer/id #uuid "473df280-9c01-54be-9ab5-5f9b35d7d479" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(54 u^{2} v^{2} + u v\\right) \\sqrt{18 u^{2} + 24 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a07bf10e-5daf-5f77-8a19-1137c0d51608" :answer/id #uuid "a07bf10e-5daf-5f77-8a19-1137c0d51608" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(- 81 u^{3} + 54 u^{2} v^{2} + u v\\right) \\left(18 u^{2} + 24 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "03e2969c-7bc4-5828-b311-0b75c71bdde5" :answer/id #uuid "03e2969c-7bc4-5828-b311-0b75c71bdde5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(- 81 u^{3} + 54 u^{2} v^{2} + u v\\right) \\sqrt{18 u^{2} + 24 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "db499b45-10a8-52f9-b982-757feb90ff5d" :answer/id #uuid "db499b45-10a8-52f9-b982-757feb90ff5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(81 u^{3} + 54 u^{2} v^{2} + u v\\right) \\sqrt{18 u^{2} + 24 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4deea122-0bc4-5c62-869f-4a630e0ddb1c" :answer-field/id #uuid "4deea122-0bc4-5c62-869f-4a630e0ddb1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["6f08a77f-a760-599a-8653-c3042e189d26" "473df280-9c01-54be-9ab5-5f9b35d7d479" "a07bf10e-5daf-5f77-8a19-1137c0d51608" "03e2969c-7bc4-5828-b311-0b75c71bdde5" "db499b45-10a8-52f9-b982-757feb90ff5d"] :answer-field/correct "03e2969c-7bc4-5828-b311-0b75c71bdde5" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "69ca8999-9b1e-5bfc-ab7f-c561489f836e" :question/id #uuid "69ca8999-9b1e-5bfc-ab7f-c561489f836e" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x - 3 y^{2} z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u v,\\,- 3 u,\\,3 u - 2 v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression? Choose an integrand equal to the required expression as a function on $D$." :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- 3 u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3 u - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v,\\,-3,\\,3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- 3 u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3 u - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,0,\\,- 4 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ v & -3 & 3 \\\\ u & 0 & - 4 v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & - 4 v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}v & 3 \\\\ u & - 4 v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}v & -3 \\\\ u & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12 v,\\,3 u + 4 v^{2},\\,3 u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨12 v,\\,3 u + 4 v^{2},\\,3 u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(12 v)^{2}+(3 u + 4 v^{2})^{2}+(3 u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18 u^{2} + 24 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x - 3 y^{2} z)\\,{|}_{x=u v\\,y=- 3 u\\,z=3 u - 2 v^{2}} \\\\  & =u v-3\\cdot (- 3 u)^{2}\\cdot (3 u - 2 v^{2}) \\\\  & =- 81 u^{3} + 54 u^{2} v^{2} + u v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\left(- 81 u^{3} + 54 u^{2} v^{2} + u v\\right) \\sqrt{18 u^{2} + 24 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["4deea122-0bc4-5c62-869f-4a630e0ddb1c"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "2b5c61b9-0f4d-5229-83c2-28dbe2298a06" :answer/id #uuid "2b5c61b9-0f4d-5229-83c2-28dbe2298a06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "058e5939-7dca-5207-a9cf-7578532c3f28" :answer/id #uuid "058e5939-7dca-5207-a9cf-7578532c3f28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1ef0898a-8678-542f-ad45-70587f8bbd8a" :answer/id #uuid "1ef0898a-8678-542f-ad45-70587f8bbd8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\left(52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}\\right)" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9f011f25-a217-5291-b94d-c478fcc9478a" :answer/id #uuid "9f011f25-a217-5291-b94d-c478fcc9478a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "11a957d3-49ef-56db-ab0f-c02857167b9b" :answer/id #uuid "11a957d3-49ef-56db-ab0f-c02857167b9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\left(18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "db2fc28a-c600-58d0-b8a2-e9ebeb14d152" :answer-field/id #uuid "db2fc28a-c600-58d0-b8a2-e9ebeb14d152" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["2b5c61b9-0f4d-5229-83c2-28dbe2298a06" "058e5939-7dca-5207-a9cf-7578532c3f28" "1ef0898a-8678-542f-ad45-70587f8bbd8a" "9f011f25-a217-5291-b94d-c478fcc9478a" "11a957d3-49ef-56db-ab0f-c02857167b9b"] :answer-field/correct "9f011f25-a217-5291-b94d-c478fcc9478a" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "3b4808cc-728c-55b7-90f8-734ae2943c4e" :question/id #uuid "3b4808cc-728c-55b7-90f8-734ae2943c4e" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=3 x - y^{2} z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u v,\\,- 3 u,\\,2 u - 2 v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression? Choose an integrand equal to the required expression as a function on $D$." :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- 3 u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 v,\\,-3,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- 3 u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 u,\\,0,\\,- 4 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 v & -3 & 2 \\\\ 2 u & 0 & - 4 v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & - 4 v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 v & 2 \\\\ 2 u & - 4 v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 v & -3 \\\\ 2 u & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12 v,\\,4 u + 8 v^{2},\\,6 u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨12 v,\\,4 u + 8 v^{2},\\,6 u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(12 v)^{2}+(4 u + 8 v^{2})^{2}+(6 u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(3 x - y^{2} z)\\,{|}_{x=2 u v\\,y=- 3 u\\,z=2 u - 2 v^{2}} \\\\  & =6 u v-1\\cdot (- 3 u)^{2}\\cdot (2 u - 2 v^{2}) \\\\  & =- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\left(- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["db2fc28a-c600-58d0-b8a2-e9ebeb14d152"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "71ff934d-be68-5886-